  "query_preview": "(Thursday through Sunday)...\nHigh pressure aloft will continue the warming trend into next\nweekend with only slight cooling on Sunday. Widespread moderate or\ngreater HeatRisk is expected for the coast and valleys for\nThursday through Sunday with widespread major HeatRisk for inland\ncoastal areas into the western San Diego County valleys for next \nweekend. \n\nHigh temperatures for next weekend will range from a few degrees \nabove average for the lower deserts to as much as 12 to 18 degrees\nabove average for the coast and valleys in San Diego County. High\ntemperatures for next weekend will range from the 80s near the \ncoast to the mid 90s to around 100 for the inland valleys with the\nlower deserts around 100. \n\nFor next weekend, low temperatures for the Orange County coastal \nplain, and for the coast and western valleys in San Diego County \nwill be mostly in the lower to mid 70s. For Friday through Sunday,\nthere could be several records tied or broken for record warm low\ntemperatures, mostly for coastal and valley locations. The\nexisting records for some of those locations was from 1997.",
